# Write an Obsidian test

Choose the layer:

- **In-memory kit** (milliseconds, default): plugin logic, commands, settings,
  vault writes, metadata. File: `{{testRoot}}/<behavior>.test.ts`.
- **Real Obsidian** (seconds per case): anything the kit cannot prove (rendering,
  host event order, real plugin manager). File: `tests/obsidian/<behavior>.obsidian.ts`.

## In-memory kit template

```ts
// @vitest-environment happy-dom
import { afterEach, expect, it, vi } from 'vitest';
vi.mock('obsidian', () => import('@test/obsidian'));
import { App } from 'obsidian';
import { createTestApp } from '@test/obsidian';
import Plugin from '<relative path>/src/main';
import manifest from '<relative path>/manifest.json';

afterEach(() => { document.body.replaceChildren(); });
it('<observable behaviour>', async () => {
  const app = new App();
  const kit = createTestApp({ app, files: { 'Inbox.md': '# Inbox\n' } });
  const plugin = new Plugin(app, manifest);
  await kit.loadPlugin(plugin);
  expect(await kit.runCommand('<command id>')).toBe(true);
  await kit.flush();
  expect(kit.read('Inbox.md')).toBe('# Inbox\n');   // exact bytes
  await kit.unloadPlugin(plugin);
  expect(kit.errors).toEqual([]);
});
```

`{{testRoot}}/plugin-host.test.ts` is a working example. API and limits:
`docs/testing/OBSIDIAN-TEST-KIT.md`. Run: `npx vitest run --config vitest.project.config.mjs <file>`.

## Real-Obsidian template

```ts
import { describe, expect } from 'vitest';
import { test } from './support/obsidian-fixture';

describe('<feature> in real Obsidian', () => {
  test('<observable behaviour>', async ({ obsidian }) => {
    await obsidian.runCommand('<command id>');   // short id, prefixed with the plugin id
    await expect.poll(() => obsidian.eval(({ app }) => app.vault.getAbstractFileByPath('New.md') !== null)).toBe(true);
    expect(obsidian.errors()).toEqual([]);
  });
});
```

Seed notes in `tests/obsidian/vault/`. Run: `npm run test:obsidian -- <file filter>`;
evidence is in `reports/obsidian/cases/`. Use `expect.poll`/`waitFor`, never sleeps.
Guide: `docs/testing/OBSIDIAN-DEV-LOOP.md`.

Assert observable behaviour (exact file bytes, commands, DOM, no errors), never
implementation details, and never loosen an assertion to make a test pass.
